{
 "type": "ObsmetrologiaIdentificationSiteCensus",
 "checkedAt": "2026-09-04T04:18:09Z",
 "packageRoot": "lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/science-services-section/services/information-science-services-section/services/math-services-section/services/obsmetrological-services-section/lib/obsmetrologia",
 "toolchain": "lake env lean",
 "method": "Lean meta program (embedded): a constant is an identification site when its own value or type directly uses Quot.sound, Quot.mk, Quot.lift, Quot.ind, Quot.rec, or a Quotient.* constructor/eliminator; a theorem inherits every site in the transitive closure of the Obsmetrologia constants it uses; one row per theorem with its site count and site list",
 "leanSource": "import Lean\nimport Obsmetrologia\nopen Lean Elab Command\n\n/-- Names whose direct use marks a stipulated identification (a quotient construction or its axiom). -/\ndef quotNames : List Name := [``Quot.sound, ``Quot.mk, ``Quot.lift, ``Quot.ind, ``Quot.rec, ``Quot.recOn, ``Quot.hrecOn, ``Quotient.mk, ``Quotient.mk', ``Quotient.sound, ``Quotient.lift, ``Quotient.ind, ``Quotient.rec, ``Quotient.recOn, ``Quotient.exact, ``Quotient.lift\u2082]\n\ndef isHouse (n : Name) : Bool := n.toString.startsWith \"Obsmetrologia.\"\n\npartial def sitesOf (env : Environment) (cache : IO.Ref (Std.HashMap Name (Array Name))) (n : Name) : IO (Array Name) := do\n  if let some s := (\u2190 cache.get).get? n then return s\n  cache.modify (\u00b7.insert n #[])  -- cycle guard\n  let some ci := env.find? n | return #[]\n  let used := ci.getUsedConstantsAsSet\n  let mut acc : Array Name := #[]\n  if used.toList.any (fun u => quotNames.contains u) then acc := acc.push n\n  for u in used.toList do\n    if isHouse u then\n      for s in (\u2190 sitesOf env cache u) do\n        if !acc.contains s then acc := acc.push s\n  cache.modify (\u00b7.insert n acc)\n  return acc\n\n#eval show CommandElabM Unit from do\n  let env \u2190 getEnv\n  let cache \u2190 IO.mkRef ({} : Std.HashMap Name (Array Name))\n  let mut sites : Std.HashSet Name := {}\n  let mut rows : Array String := #[]\n  for (n, ci) in env.constants.toList do\n    if isHouse n && !n.isInternal then\n      let s \u2190 sitesOf env cache n\n      for x in s do sites := sites.insert x\n      if let .thmInfo _ := ci then\n        rows := rows.push s!\"{n}\\t{s.size}\\t{String.intercalate \",\" (s.map toString).toList}\"\n  IO.println s!\"#sites\\t{sites.size}\"\n  for x in (sites.toArray.qsort (fun a b => a.toString < b.toString)) do IO.println s!\"#site\\t{x}\"\n  for r in rows.qsort (\u00b7 < \u00b7) do IO.println r\n",
 "law": "Owner-ruled 2026-09-03 (this session, verbatim intent): the library is meant to spend Quot.sound one time, at the articulating spiral initially, and everything downstream inherits that one identification; in Lean, how many independent identifications a theorem inherits is the difference between its being settled and postulated. This law is the corpus's own, not the public literature's.",
 "reading": "Measured against that law: 118 independent identification sites exist; none is at the root (Primitive/Mark.lean and Articulation/Articulating.lean construct no quotient; Articulating is a plain inductive). 7,612 of 8,308 theorems inherit no site at all (they never identify); 696 inherit one or more, and 652 of those inherit two or more. 79 of the 118 sites sit in Calculus/Real (the internal rationals and reals are quotient stacks: Rat.mk is inherited by 595 theorems), 14 in Positing/Bigraded, 11 in AperiodicOrder, 6 in Ord, 4 in Algebra, 3 in Thermodynamics, 1 in CausalSets. So the H-theorem (Thermodynamics.htheorem) inherits 28 sites, all through the internal reals, while reconnection_event_implies_H1_nonzero, timeSection_strict_mono and prBox_hasGlobalSection_iff inherit none. The discharge the law names is structural, not per-theorem: introduce the one root identification and refactor the internal reals so their identifications are derived from it (the setoid-reals refactor named 2026-07-11), after which the site count becomes the settled/postulated measure the law intends.",
